*getterm* | V-$CHIPVR ($CHIPCN)

''getterm()''

Returns the current termios state for the controlling terminal.

*Returns:*
- Map: termios state
- ''err'' on failure

*Map fields:*
- ''"iflag"'' (Number): input mode flags
- ''"oflag"'' (Number): output mode flags
- ''"cflag"'' (Number): control mode flags
- ''"lflag"'' (Number): local mode flags
- ''"line"'' (Number): line discipline
- ''"ispeed"'' (Number): input baud rate
- ''"ospeed"'' (Number): output baud rate
- ''"VINTR"'' (Number): interrupt character
- ''"VQUIT"'' (Number): quit character
- ''"VERASE"'' (Number): erase character
- ''"VKILL"'' (Number): kill character
- ''"VEOF"'' (Number): end-of-file character
- ''"VTIME"'' (Number): non-canonical read timeout (deciseconds)
- ''"VMIN"'' (Number): non-canonical minimum characters per read
- ''"VSWTC"'' (Number): switch character
- ''"VSTART"'' (Number): start-output character
- ''"VSTOP"'' (Number): stop-output character
- ''"VSUSP"'' (Number): suspend character
- ''"VEOL"'' (Number): end-of-line character
- ''"VREPRINT"'' (Number): reprint character
- ''"VDISCARD"'' (Number): discard character
- ''"VWERASE"'' (Number): word-erase character
- ''"VLNEXT"'' (Number): literal-next character
- ''"VEOL2"'' (Number): alternate end-of-line character
